+# smallpt — Light, traced.
+
+Kevin Beason’s open-source C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly, with a responsive static browser interface. Rendering runs on the visitor’s CPU in a dedicated module Web Worker; it does not call a rendering service or require cross-origin isolation headers.
+
+Open `index.html` through your existing static hosting environment. ES modules and WebAssembly need HTTP(S); opening the file directly with `file://` is unsupported. The checked-in `wasm/` artifacts are ready to serve, so Emscripten is only required to rebuild them.
+
+## Build
+
+With [Emscripten](https://emscripten.org/docs/getting_started/downloads.html) installed and its environment activated:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+This compiles `src/smallpt.cpp` with `em++` and writes the deployable static site to `dist/`. Set `EMXX` to use a compiler at a custom path. No npm dependencies are needed for the build.
+
+```sh
+npm run build:preview
+npm run build
+```
+
+The optional preview build runs the **actual compiled WebAssembly in Node**, checks output opacity, deterministic seeds, palette changes (including both spheres), and image dimension limits, then generates `assets/preview.png`. It reads the binary directly without starting a server. The static preview provides an initial image while the live renderer loads; the browser automatically begins a fresh render.
+
+## Controls
+
+- **Randomize & render** changes the reflectance colors of both walls and both interior spheres, selects a new seed, and starts a fresh render.
+- **Render scene** uses the selected resolution and quality with the current palette. While rendering, this button stops the job. Starting a new job also cancels the previous one.
+- **Reset** restores the original Cornell box palette, 640 × 480 resolution, 64 samples per pixel, and seed 42.
+- **Save image** exports the current live canvas as PNG after its first full sampling pass.
+- The expand icon opens the output in fullscreen where supported.
+
+## Source and license
+
+Original project: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
+
+The unmodified source and MIT license are retained in `vendor/smallpt/`. The browser adaptation retains Kevin Beason’s sphere intersection, scene geometry, camera, diffuse/specular/refractive radiance functions, Russian roulette, and 2 × 2 tent-filtered sampling. It replaces OpenMP and PPM file output with a progressive linear-radiance accumulator, bounded color randomization, and a contiguous RGBA buffer shared with JavaScript. Accumulated radiance is clamped and gamma-corrected for display after averaging.
+
+`render-worker.js` processes short row batches, transfers pixel buffers, and allows cancellation between batches. `app.js` owns the canvas and controls. All scene computation takes place in C++ / WebAssembly; JavaScript coordinates jobs and displays pixels.
